{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>מקצר</b> is defective (lacking vav) and its numerical value equals ת\"ל (470), to teach that at the end of ת\"ל years they went out, as stated: ויהי מקץ שלשים שנה וארבע מאות שנה." "<b>(</b> (3) ויצום. Four times in the Masorah: ויצום וגו' אל פרעה — and afterward נגשו בני ישראל. ויצום את כל אשר דבר. ויצום לאמר זה הדבר אשר תעשון — regarding Jehoiada who brought out the king's son. ויצום לאמר לא תיראו אלהים אחרים — regarding the king of Assyria, in the pericope of the Samaritans, when the lions killed among them. In the merit of Moses, who was sent as emissary of HaShem to command Israel — and just as the commands there dealt with idolatry (that of the king of Assyria) and bloodshed (that of Jehoiada, who commanded to kill the queen), so here Moses commands to distance from idolatry and from bloodshed."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The Hebrew paraphrases Ezekiel 4:6 but writes the sum as ת״ל (400+30 = 430) rather than spelling out the total; the verse cited reads 'at the end of thirty years and four hundred years.' The gematria of מקצר (defective) = 470 = ת״ל."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:08.846968281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}